Magicbane and artifact selection strategy spoiler says:

"What is the best enchantment for Magicbane?  If you simply want to
cause the most damage, then the table indicates that you should enchant
it as high as possible (safely to +7).  Fortunately, your odds of magic-
resistance, curse-resistance, and engraving do not depend upon the
enchantment."


It also gives the following average damage done by Magicbane at +2 and
+7 enchantments:

  At +2 Magicbane averages  9.48 dmg
  At +7 Magicbane averages 13.4  dmg.




  That's four more points of damage.  What is a +4 ring of increase
damage worth to you?  What if it had no nutrition cost and didn't take
up a ring slot?  That's what enchanting up Magicbane will do for you.


  Magicbane's special effects are probe, stun, scare, confuse, cancel.

  - Probe is almost completely useless.
  - Stun gives +2 to hit on the monster for a few turns.  
  - Scare is useless compared to Magicbane's Elbereth engraving
  - Confuse is useless compared to Magicbane's Elbereth engraving
  - Cancel is only tried 10% of the time at best.  Over half of the
    monsters have nothing to cancel.  The others its useless, too late
    at melee range (disenchanters, rust monsters, nymphs, etc.) or can
    be resisted.  Once again engraving Elbereth works much better.

  Engraving Elbereth will work on all surrounding squares.  You can
leave an item on the Elbereth and it will keep working on all
surrounding squares.


  The chances of a given effect per hit based on enchantment:

  ENCHANT  NORMAL  PROBE  STUN   SCARE   CANCL  MAGIC AVE DMG
